course: dictionary
lesson: 4948
title: Imprison and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Imprison means to put someone in prison, or to keep them locked up so they cannot leave. It is a verb, so it describes an action.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «Paul travelled across the Roman world starting churches, and was shipwrecked, beaten and imprisoned.» Shipwrecked and beaten are bad things that happen to a person, so imprisoned is bad too. It must mean locked up.
explain: Imprison is not only about prisons. In stories a villain may imprison a hero in a tower. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Locked up, trapped and unable to leave is a good fit, so you have your meaning.
fact: Imprison is a verb. Its forms are imprison, imprisons, imprisoned and imprisoning.
fact: «Imprisoned» means put in prison or kept locked up, so someone cannot leave.
fact: You may see the phrases be imprisoned for a crime, imprisoned in a tower, and wrongly imprisoned.
fact: «Wrongly imprisoned» means locked up unfairly, even though the person had done nothing wrong.
exercise: «Paul was shipwrecked, beaten and imprisoned.» What does imprisoned mean here? | Given a present | *Put in prison or locked up | Washed safely ashore | Sent on a holiday
exercise: The Rat lists what Toad has been: «handcuffed, imprisoned, starved, chased». Which word means put in prison? | handcuffed | starved | *imprisoned | chased
exercise: In stories a villain may imprison a hero in a tower. What does imprison mean? | *Keep someone trapped so they cannot leave | Fly high above | Give a warm welcome to | Read a book about
test: The guards ___ the thief last night. Which form fits? | imprisons | imprison | *imprisoned | imprisoning
test: Which phrase means locked up even though the person had done nothing wrong? | *Wrongly imprisoned | Hungry in a tall tower | Chased across the moor | Be freed for good behaviour
exam: Which sentence uses imprisoned correctly? | Mum imprisoned the sunshine in her bag | The dog imprisoned a ball in the garden | The baker imprisoned three loaves of bread on the shelf | *The king imprisoned the rebels in the castle dungeon
